      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:150mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q04-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Adjacent triangles ABD and BCD.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABD\"></span> and triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BCD\"></span></p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ADC\"></span> is a straight line</li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BD = (x + 3) \\text{ cm}\"></span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC = x \\text{ cm}\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BDC = 30^\\circ\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BCD = 140^\\circ\"></span></li></ul><p>(a) show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = 10.5\"></span> correct to 3 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>Given also that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AD = (x - 2) \\text{ cm}\"></span></p><p>(b) find the length of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
