    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = \\frac{6}{x} + 3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(a) (i) Sketch <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> stating the coordinates of any points where the curve cuts the coordinate axes.</p><p>(ii) State the equations of any asymptotes to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> has equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = 3x^2 - 4x - 10\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(b) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> intersect when</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3x^3 - 4x^2 - 13x - 6 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Given that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of one of the points of intersection is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{2}{3}\"></span></p><p>(c) use algebra to find the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinates of the other points of intersection between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span></p><p>(Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.)</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
