    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q6",
      "question": "<p>The binomial expansion of</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(1 + ax)^{12}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>up to and including the term in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2\"></span> is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1 - \\frac{15}{2} x + kx^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> are constants.</p><p>(a) Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a = -\\frac{5}{8}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) Hence find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Using the expansion and making your method clear,</p><p>(c) find an estimate for the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac{17}{16}\\right)^{12}\"></span>, giving your answer to 4 decimal places.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
