    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q7",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:95mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q07-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Linear graph of log concentration against distance.\"></figure><p>A chimney emits smoke particles.</p><p>On a particular day, the concentration of smoke particles in the air emitted by this chimney, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> parts per million, is measured at various distances, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> km, from the chimney.</p><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of the linear relationship between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10} P\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> that is used to model this situation.</p><p>The line passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0, 3.3)\"></span> and the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6, 2.1)\"></span></p><p>(a) Find a complete equation for the model in the form</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"P = ab^x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants. Give the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> each to 4 significant figures.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) With reference to the model, interpret the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ab\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
