    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q8",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:100mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q08-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Shaded region between the cubic and tangent.\"></figure><p>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</p><p>Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p>Figure 3 shows a sketch of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = x^3 - 14x + 23\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is the tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, also shown in Figure 3.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = -2x + 7\"></span></p><p>(a) show, using calculus, that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> is 2</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> cuts <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> again at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>.</p><p>(b) Verify that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The finite region, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 3, is bounded by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>.</p><p>Using algebraic integration,</p><p>(c) show that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is 108</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
