      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q10",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:83mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q10-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4. Circle and tangent at Q.\"></figure><p>Figure 4 shows a sketch of the circle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></p><ul><li>the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1, k + 8\"></span>) is the centre of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> (<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3, k^2 - 2k\"></span>) lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a positive constant</li></ul><ul><li>the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is the tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span></li></ul><p>Given that the gradient of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2\"></span></p><p>(a) show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"k^2 - 3k - 10 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(b) Hence find an equation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
