      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q12",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:80mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2024-june/q12-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 5. Plan of the swimming pool.\"></figure><p>Figure 5 shows the plan view of the design for a swimming pool.</p><p>The pool is modelled as a quarter of a circle joined to two equal sized rectangles as shown.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>the quarter circle has radius <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> metres</li></ul><ul><li>the rectangles each have length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> metres and width <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> metres</li></ul><ul><li>the total surface area of the swimming pool is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"100\\text{ m}^2\"></span></li></ul><p>(a) show that, according to the model, the perimeter <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> metres of the swimming pool is given by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"P = 2x + \\frac{200}{x}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p><p>(b) Use calculus to find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> for which <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> has a stationary value.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(c) Prove, by further calculus, that this value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> gives a minimum value for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>Access to the pool is by side <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span> shown in Figure 5.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span> must be at least one metre,</p><p>(d) determine, according to the model, whether the swimming pool with the minimum perimeter would be suitable.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
